<PageTitle>Python client docs: DbnSuite</PageTitle>

<h1>Python client</h1>
<p class="lead">
    Read an archive, and DbnTape tapes, from Python: list and fetch days by the layout's rules, load tapes into numpy
    or pandas, and deal Monte Carlo sessions exactly as C# does.
</p>

<div class="note warn"><p>
    <strong>Contributed and largely untested.</strong> Its tests check it against the C# code on synthetic tapes and a
    stand-in archive, but nobody has yet used it for real research. It needs people who work in Python to adopt it,
    review it, try it on their own archives and tapes, and say what's wrong or missing, in
    <a href="@Links.PythonIssues">issues with the python label</a> or a pull request. Expect its API to change. Use it
    at your own risk.
</p></div>

